module gunbc.plans.host_effect_orchestration

import std.dissolution { unbound_dissolution }
import gunbc.plan { Plan, PlanRetirement, PlanRetiresWhen, PlanIsAuthorityOnly }
import std.markdown { MarkdownBlock }
import gunbc.plans.md_helpers { p }
import gunbc.design_ruling { project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts }

fn host_effect_orchestration_body() -> List<MarkdownBlock> {
  [
    p(text: "Goal (operator 2026-06-24): one .dag install/manage/decommission lifecycle, hosts bootstrapping/pulling desired state with minimal central dependencies, and ctrl responsibilities deleted as they migrate. This is the historical model/sign-off record; later carrier rulings govern current execution. Shell artifact/thin-run and interpreter SSH are realizations of one interface, not competing regimes."),
    p(text: "apply combines independent target/control plane, effect kind, transport and drive policy. HostOs and BmcController bind fleet_intent identities; RunnerLocalHost is a separate foreign-executor subject admitting only modeled local effects, never fabricated fleet identity. Pre-OS operations require out-of-band control. HostEffect is a coproduct of typed operations, not a universal command string; incompatible effect/transport cells refuse by construction. Dispatch belongs at realization boundaries."),
    p(text: "Receipt reuses Reconciliation<HostEffectIntent,HostEffectEvidence>, generalizing #5725’s locked located/typed core with its owner instead of forking grammar. Evidence is domain payload; Reconciliation relates it to intent, so they must not collapse. Async Redfish acknowledgment is not boot success: observe/poll terminal change, including consumption of one-time boot override. Host/control vocabulary stays with its product owner; std.effects owns generic EffectShape, extdeps owns spec-grounded transports. Folder-direction convention is not a new import law."),
    p(text: "Effect-plan ruling 2026-07-03: one std.effect_plan composition authority replaces v2.std.orchestration naming. Bounded seq/If/While/Retry/FailurePolicy compose Do\{effect\} leaves. Substrate owns control/termination; extdeps owns typed operations and transport argv; host_effect owns target/intent/evidence; upsert_decision owns observation/classification/remedy; temporal_effect owns durable attempts/leases/approval; media grammars own rendering. A new command/process/evidence/policy type must prove a distinct responsibility or name its de-fork."),
    p(text: "Policy correction: OneShotIdempotent duplicated EffectShape’s idempotency fact. HostEffectIntent uses existing IdempotencyEvidence; only derived Drive OneShot/ConvergeLoop remains, targeting the construction-first v2 EffectShape partition without a third interim axis. upsert_decision subsumes temporal HeldLeaseObservedState/NextStepPlan and os_install plan classification; PlanAwaitApproval remains temporal residue and OS preflight verdicts stay domain-specific. Refusal reasons and EffectStepReceipt verdict/plan labels become typed; #6193 fired the latter dissolution."),
    p(text: "In-attempt Retry mitigation ladder differs from durable receipt-mediated convergence; never merge them. While requires a measure and derives DescentEvidence from std.termination, not authored descent; absent measure is unconstructible. Wire or narrow Retry.on_exhausted before cutover. Later lowering to ordinary substrate fragments may dissolve reified EffectPlan only when leaves/transport/policy/receipt facts survive; it remains the near-term bounded construction wall. Delete unconsumed RetryCount; resolve inert TemporalEffectPolicy before consumers; ground workflow RetryDue/Retryable when wired and HostExecArgv into existing git/tmux/claude operations before another consumer."),
    p(text: "Terminal topology: host pulls content-addressed desired state and reconciles locally; center emits intent and performs initial BMC bootstrap. BMC VirtualMedia/PXE according to observed capability→autoinstall→on-host agent. PXE needs firmware network stack/same L2 and does not cross overlay; recorded srv3 OpenBMC 2.07 VirtualMedia support does not imply general PXE reach. Interface stays mechanism-agnostic."),
    p(text: "Phase A landed #5756: shared host_effect shape/target and total realization fold, actual LocalShell exit evidence, typed incompatible cells and fail-closed Redfish Unimplemented; existing Reconciliation outcome and real-execution/red controls. Raw ShellCommand script was admitted interim debt, not the terminal shape. Interface/signature/arms were co-owned smart-newt-512/neat-boar-71 with receipt owner fierce-carp; not separately minted."),
    p(text: "B follows proven srv3 OsInstalled: migrate every host_exec in one pass, then dissolve script payload jointly with source strings into effect-plan intent. Most strings are typed process invocations—extend existing extdeps service operations, never new std.ProcessInvocation; Pipeline composes, Bash appears at realization edges. shell_emission_model supersedes deleted program.dag sidecar (#6831). C realizes typed BMC boot override/reset and independent polling through RedfishRest."),
    p(text: "D models EmitArtifactThenThinRun as a handler, deletes ctrl runner_host_reconcile hash/fanout and defaultContainerResourceCaps, and emits typed receipts; an opaque imperative binary is no improvement. E installs self-convergence via autoinstall/systemd and removes steady-state SSH-star dependence. F reverses lifecycle through drain→deregister offers→revoke credentials→secure erase→BMC off/reset. Until a real decommission consumer earns implementation, typed Unimplemented stubs refuse, never plausible no-op success."),
    p(text: "Validate one interface/fleet authority/receipt grammar through end-to-end lifecycle execution after seam migration; drop-required-input and decommission-stub controls must refuse. Measure displaced ctrl responsibility/LOC, not added code. Historical phase labels/standing do not authorize restoring now-retired emitters or bypassing current seed-maintenance rules."),
  ]
}

data host_effect_orchestration_plan: Plan = Plan {
  projection: PlanIsAuthorityOnly { ruling: project_documentation_projections_are_not_checkout_artifacts },
  slug: "host-effect-orchestration",
  title: "Host-effect orchestration — interface + shell→.dag migration plan",
  body: host_effect_orchestration_body(),
  retirement: PlanRetiresWhen { condition: unbound_dissolution(description: "Delete this doc when the `apply(target, effect, policy) -> Receipt` interface is minted in product (the `HostEffect` coproduct + `NodeControlPlane` co-owned as one unit), every `host_exec()` call is migrated onto it, the BMC `RedfishAction` arm over `RedfishRest` and the converge-lane `EmitArtifactThenThinRun` handler have landed, ctrl host-apply LOC (the `runner_host_reconcile.mjs` hash/fan-out + `defaultContainerResourceCaps`) is deleted, and the on-host self-converge policy + the decom reverse-fold are realized (or their fail-closed `Unimplemented` stubs are witnessed) — at which point the lifecycle is one tested interface and this design note is redundant.")
  }
}
